% On SMTimer with Z3, our method increases successfully solved instances from 72 to 94 (+30.6\%) while reducing average solving time from 561s to 214s (2.6$\times$ speedup). The gains generalize across solver architectures: CVC5 achieves +57.9\% improvement, BVParti shows +850\% relative improvement, and MathSAT demonstrates +244.8\% enhancement. Particularly compelling is the method's ability to convert previously intractable cases—on \QFNIA{}, \tool enables Z3 to successfully solve 324 instances that previously timed out under the same 1200s budget. These results indicate that policy-driven, semantics-aware concretization can transform otherwise unsolvable formulas into manageable ones while preserving solver independence across different architectures.

