The main contributions of this paper are as follows:
\begin{itemize}
  \item We formalize \SMT{} constraint simplification as a sequential decision-making problem and present \tool, an AI-assisted framework that synergistically combines policy learning via \RL{} with semantic synthesis via \LLM{}. Our dual-agent architecture decomposes the complex action space: a strategic \RL{} agent selects high-impact variables for concretization, while an \LLM{} generates semantically appropriate values. This design enables strategic planning through learned policies rather than brittle heuristics. \wyc{too long, need to simplify.}
